{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/1573b4e4d50ce9da8b589bcd281c82a0449e8d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 5x^2 + ax + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3466d6567c8c74894098c7046a69ebfe17fd8ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> as a root. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c651391bd14d67f7ff5f5123a74bd65fd5a1dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 13 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 17 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 30 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because every coefficient of our polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is an integer, the conjugate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3466d6567c8c74894098c7046a69ebfe17fd8ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb4077f21bea3549b4544757a7dfb723515c6c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> is also a root. \n</p><p>Let the third and final root be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae5f496b8ddda88b5cbbc06ccb02bee0580fd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Thanks to Vieta's Formulas, we know that the sum of the roots is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c193e1c9dfd296af6142c00da515e6b11da330.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(r_3) + (4+\\sqrt{5}) + (4 - \\sqrt{5}) = 5\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791388f0b7f5bbcea9c4f03aec39108b1bcd6a71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_3 = -3.\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We now calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b8d088c91ce4d4db97ee973f672ed5c766a59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = (1+3)(1-4-\\sqrt{5})(1-4+\\sqrt{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"317\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/79687beab8e6c1e5547592d738cb4428db461a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-4-\\sqrt{5})(1-4+\\sqrt{5}) = (-3-\\sqrt{5})(-3+\\sqrt{5}) = 9 - 5 = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"499\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f301cc6efa42916602dafd2fdbaad856fe4d3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 4 \\cdot 4 = 16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f94ac573e3776311498cf80182aa3544afcf515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 16 = 1-5 + a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034cec4c618d0d73e8283a3736cba8cbe55f9d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = \\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~lprado (minor edits by singularity1)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> contains roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3466d6567c8c74894098c7046a69ebfe17fd8ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> and its conjugate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb4077f21bea3549b4544757a7dfb723515c6c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a9900d3e41143e7229501b3bbef2a43932d833ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3=-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae5f496b8ddda88b5cbbc06ccb02bee0580fd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is the last root. Hence, we can create a factorization for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and compare coefficients as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022e70492c4a36680fb771af38cca34f1bafa474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+3)(x-(4+\\sqrt{5}))(x-(4-\\sqrt{5}))=(x+3)(x^2-8x+11)=x^3-8x^2+11x+3x^2-24x+33=x^3-5x^3-13x+33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"950\" height=\"24\" />, and hence by comparing the coefficients we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e14d0da2b4d10b77e5bc962f1e820b632c126b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=-13+33=\\boxed{20\\hspace{1mm}\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"226\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~singularity1\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Bash)\">Solution 3 (Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd31a5677d3a8c282b5661e56614193974917b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+\\sqrt{ 5 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> is a root of polynomial, by definition\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a57705a7047a757e0c8e5cbbb0a97fb682e674b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(4+\\sqrt{ 5 })^3-5(4+\\sqrt{ 5 })^2+a(4+\\sqrt{ 5 })+b=0=0+0\\sqrt { 5 }\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"21\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e61e4642659c51c8d8a998ed545b99282987d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />, we can expand and compare coefficients,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df4493f5f18b5804b182b8fed01701d27705c2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} 64+3\\cdot 4 \\cdot 5-5(4^2+5)+4a+b=0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 16+5-5\\cdot 2\\cdot 4+a=0 \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"53\" />\nSolving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/16996bc4909a91e3dbc85726a28198a294112f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4ae69511fba3f17c7eb20af0b2f9bd11489966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=-4a-19=33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c9083068ab0d771a0c142eec19b8f20583877e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~imosilver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just find the terms that have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> in them to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then only look at the integer terms to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(I know this way works but can smn else write the actual math to get the answer)\n</p><p>~vaishnav\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As explained in earlier solutions the given function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/1573b4e4d50ce9da8b589bcd281c82a0449e8d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 5x^2 + ax + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3466d6567c8c74894098c7046a69ebfe17fd8ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3466d6567c8c74894098c7046a69ebfe17fd8ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb4077f21bea3549b4544757a7dfb723515c6c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore it should be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6967220880ca7650beeef9a177bdfe1349863b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4+\\sqrt{5})(4-\\sqrt{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"24\" /> with no remainder.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486fd8a401c7be773ee551bf999df3e739489ff1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(4+\\sqrt{5})(4-\\sqrt{5})=x^2-8x+11\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e686eca129b754296e5a623d5a8c2f3684a9e426.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{rll}     &amp;\\phantom{x^3 - 5x^2 + a}x + 3\\\\   \\cline{2-3}   x^2 - 8x + 11 &amp; \\multicolumn{2}{|l}{x^3 - 5x^2 + ax + b} \\\\     &amp; \\underline{-(x^3 - 8x^2 + 11x)} \\\\     &amp; \\phantom{x^3 + } 3x^2 + (a-11)x + b \\\\     &amp; \\underline{\\phantom{x^3} - (3x^2 - 24x + 33)} \\\\     &amp; \\phantom{x^3 + 3x^2 + } (a+13)x + (b-33) \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"121\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e824ae482056155932b852664848ad29b63d1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+13)x + (b-33)=0\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\nSo in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/648c529664f883f50836af741f02424c4430777e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+13)x + (b-33)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf1a33c2dfe83bdb75d948f682de4e2e8267ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />&amp;<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/6911134038615f6aac866983f2e94bc376d12bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-33)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> must each equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/92111db0aaaf2e69b5ad605e19302bfa94fb4974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a=-13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e59d7add53f1e89b30ab5789b7ff82b6b1ac3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b=33)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c9083068ab0d771a0c142eec19b8f20583877e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~vig\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B\">2025 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/